// Issue #734: build a classification in one view and apply it in another.
//
// Menu items are addressed by the left part of their caption rather than by position, so that
// entries added or removed above them cannot silently make this script fire something else.
// A name that matches nothing, or that matches more than one item, is reported as an error.
//
// Run with MicroTst.dms. Expected in the log:
//   - one "ts <n> is caused by ClassBreaks_ApplyToItems" per in-place paste (one epoch tick),
//   - one "ts <n> is caused by ClassBreaks_ApplyToLayer" for the regenerating paste,
//   - "PasteClassBreaks: the classification of hoek_centroid is configured or calculated and
//      was left unchanged; a new one was generated for this view",
//   - "Cannot paste class break -300 into class breaks of type uint32" when the int32 breaks of
//      hoek are pasted onto the uint32 hoek_centroid,
//   - no other errors.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- generated classification
// hoek has no cdf, so the map view generates its class attributes under /Desktops/...:
// pasting must overwrite them in place and round-trip losslessly.
ActivateItem "/BackGroundLayer/district/hoek"
DefaultView
WAIT 8000

SEND 4 2 1 "Copy Classbreaks"
WAIT 1500

SEND 4 2 1 "Paste Classbreaks"
WAIT 3000

SEND 4 2 1 "Copy Classbreaks"
WAIT 1500

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- the palette editor route
SEND 4 2 1 "Edit Palette"
WAIT 3000

SEND 4 2 1 "Paste Classbreaks"
WAIT 3000

SEND 4 2 1 "Copy Classbreaks"
WAIT 1500

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- config classification
// hoek_centroid has cdf = "hoek_classes/classBreaks", which is configured and shared. Pasting
// the int32 breaks of hoek must be refused on the value type before anything is created.
ActivateItem "/BackGroundLayer/district/hoek_centroid"
DefaultView
WAIT 8000

SEND 4 2 1 "Paste Classbreaks"
WAIT 3000

// Copying and pasting hoek_centroid onto itself does fit uint32: the configured items must stay
// untouched and the layer must be re-themed onto a freshly generated, editable classification.
SEND 4 2 1 "Copy Classbreaks"
WAIT 1500

SEND 4 2 1 "Paste Classbreaks"
WAIT 4000

SEND 4 2 1 "Copy Classbreaks"
WAIT 1500

SEND 1 3 16 0 0
